===============================================================================
SCOPE OF THIS LICENSE
===============================================================================

The MIT license above covers only the files original to this repository:

    build_ffmpeg.sh, build_ffmpeg_macos.sh, package_windows.ps1,
    package_macos.sh, generate_bindings.ps1, bindgen-config/,
    hand-written/, windows-deps.lock, README.md

    libraw/build_libraw.ps1, libraw/build_libraw_macos.sh,
    libraw/generate_bindings.ps1, libraw/bindgen-config/, libraw/README.md

    zeiger/build_ffmpeg.sh, zeiger/README.md

It does NOT cover:

  * ffmpeg/ (git submodule) -- FFmpeg, licensed LGPL-2.1-or-later under its own
    terms. See ffmpeg/COPYING.LGPLv2.1 and ffmpeg/LICENSE.md.

  * odin-c-bindgen/ (git submodule) -- licensed under its own terms upstream.

  * lgpl-sources/ -- unmodified upstream source tarballs for LAME, libsoxr,
    FriBidi and GNU libiconv, each licensed LGPL under its own terms. They are
    included to satisfy the corresponding-source obligation for those libraries,
    which are statically linked into the FFmpeg libraries Blick ships.

  * The generated Odin bindings in output/, which are produced mechanically from
    FFmpeg's public headers. Per LGPL-2.1 section 5, a work using only numerical
    parameters, data structure layouts and accessors from a library's headers is
    unrestricted regardless of whether it is legally a derivative work, so these
    are distributed under the MIT terms above.

  * libraw/source/ -- the unmodified upstream source tarballs:
      - LibRaw, offered under LGPL-2.1 or CDDL-1.0; Dihedron Software uses it
        under the CDDL 1.0. See LICENSE.CDDL and COPYRIGHT inside the tarball.
      - zlib, licensed under the zlib license. See LICENSE inside the tarball.
      - libjpeg-turbo, licensed under the IJG license and the BSD-3-Clause
        license. See LICENSE.md and README.ijg inside the tarball.
    zlib and libjpeg-turbo are compiled into the LibRaw library for deflate
    and lossy DNG files.

  * libraw/output/LICENSE.CDDL, COPYRIGHT, LICENSE.zlib,
    LICENSE.libjpeg-turbo.md and README.ijg -- copied unmodified from the
    tarballs above by the build.

  * The generated Odin bindings in libraw/output/, which are produced from
    LibRaw's headers. The CDDL has no equivalent of LGPL-2.1 section 5, so these
    are distributed under the CDDL 1.0, the same as LibRaw. See
    libraw/output/LICENSE.CDDL and libraw/output/COPYRIGHT.
